@@ -45,9 +45,9 @@ One term per thing. The supervisor, the subagents, and every brief use these ter
 | **Product type** | How a product reaches its user: where it runs, how it is delivered, and what its main interface is (a web app, a video game, a host extension). Each part has exactly one, fixed at intake, from the open list. |
 | **Sub-type** | A narrower kind within one product type (a Roblox game within video games; a Claude Code extension within host extensions), with a workflow of its own because it changes a phase, a gate, a check or the tooling. A part has at most one sub-type, of its own product type. |
 | **Trait** | A property that adds work whatever the product type (has screens, installable, spends money). A part may have any number, proposed at intake and settled at the design gate, from the open list. |
-| **Conditional workflow** | The collective name for a type workflow, a sub-workflow or a trait addition: a small file that changes the main workflow only at extension points; everything it does not mention is inherited. It can never remove a founding rule, weaken the merge gate, or skip the requirements register, the inventory or the reviews. |
-| **Type workflow** | The main workflow adapted to one product type: its changes at named extension points (`workflow/types/<type>.md`). It may add, replace and set. |
-| **Sub-workflow** | A more detailed version of a type workflow for one sub-type (`workflow/types/<type>/<sub-type>.md`): it inherits its type workflow and changes only what differs, at the same extension points, and may override its type workflow's replacement or setting. |
+| **Conditional workflow** | The collective name for a type workflow, a sub-workflow or a trait addition: a small file that changes the main workflow only by adding or setting at extension points or, for a type workflow or a sub-workflow, by replacing a whole phase module the registry marks replaceable; everything it does not mention is inherited. It can never remove a founding rule, weaken the merge gate, or skip the requirements register, the inventory or the reviews. |
+| **Type workflow** | The main workflow adapted to one product type (`workflow/types/<type>.md`): it adds and sets at named extension points, and may replace a whole phase module the registry marks replaceable. |
+| **Sub-workflow** | A more detailed version of a type workflow for one sub-type (`workflow/types/<type>/<sub-type>.md`): it inherits its type workflow and changes only what differs, adding and setting at the same extension points or replacing the same replaceable modules, and may override its type workflow's replacement or setting. |
 | **Trait addition** | What one trait adds to the procedure (`workflow/traits/<trait>.md`), whatever the product type. A trait addition may only add, never replace or set, so any combination of traits composes. |
 | **Add** | As a kind of change a conditional workflow makes: extra content at an extension point (questions, sections, diagram kinds, checks, brief constraints, stages, completion conditions, reflection items) beside what is already there. Additions from several conditional workflows apply together, in the order the core states. |
 | **Replace** | As a kind of change a conditional workflow makes: a whole phase module substituted, only where the registry marks the module replaceable; only a type workflow or a sub-workflow may replace. |
